title: A Leadership Challenge
tags: event
priority: 3
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and in_campaign = 0 and time - leadership_challenge_time >= 12 and ((thatcher_rating < 20 and dissent >= 0.35) or (rebellion >= 10 and thatcher_rating < 40) or falklands = 4)
new-page: true
on-arrival: leadership_challenge_time = time

= A Leadership Challenge

[? if falklands = 4 : After the South Atlantic disaster, ?][? if falklands != 4 : With the party in revolt and the polls dire, ?] a senior backbencher announces he will stand against you for the leadership. He's a stalking horse: if you are weakened in the first ballot, the real contenders will come in for the second.

- @fight: Fight it on your record.
- @concessions: Buy off the wets with a change of course first.
- @resign: Resign rather than face the humiliation.

@fight
on-arrival: {!
var support = 62 + 0.5 * (Q.thatcher_rating - 30) - 30 * (Q.dissent - 0.2) - 1 * Q.rebellion;
if (Q.falklands == 3) {
    support += 20;
}
if (Q.falklands == 4) {
    support -= 15;
}
Q.challenge_support = Math.round(support);
Q.survived = (support + (Math.random() - 0.5) * 10 >= 50) ? 1 : 0;
!}
go-to: survived if survived = 1; ousted if survived = 0

@concessions
on-arrival: {!
Q.wet_dissent -= 15;
Q.dry_dissent += 10;
Q.economic_liberalism -= 4;
Q.spending += 1;
Q.budget -= 2;
var support = 68 + 0.5 * (Q.thatcher_rating - 30) - 30 * (Q.dissent - 0.2) - 1 * Q.rebellion;
if (Q.falklands == 4) {
    support -= 15;
}
Q.challenge_support = Math.round(support);
Q.survived = (support + (Math.random() - 0.5) * 10 >= 50) ? 1 : 0;
!}
go-to: survived if survived = 1; ousted if survived = 0

You promise a "review" of economic strategy, more for the regions, and a seat at the table for the wets.

@survived
on-arrival: rebellion -= 4; wet_dissent -= 5; loyalist_dissent -= 5; thatcher_rating += 3

You win the ballot comfortably enough that no one else enters. The rebellion is over, for now.

@ousted
on-arrival: ousted = 1; con_in_government = 0
go-to: game_over

Too many abstentions. The men in grey suits tell you that you cannot win a second ballot. You withdraw, and the party chooses a new leader.

@resign
on-arrival: ousted = 1; con_in_government = 0
go-to: game_over

You announce that you will not put the party through a contest, and that you will resign as soon as a successor is chosen.
